<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_p2p",
    "Revoke sits beside the address on any Share bar — a conference, a space, a P2P session, a game. It stops the link working, and it stops nothing else."
  )}
</p>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_protocol_conference_compact}>
  {dgettext("help_p2p", "The room is untouched")}
</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_p2p",
    "Whoever is already inside stays inside, and anybody who can reach the room another way still can. Only the address dies. A card already sitting in a conversation stops offering a way in, and following the old link from anywhere else says the link is no longer active."
  )}
</p>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_btn_link}>{dgettext("help_p2p", "One address per room")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_p2p",
    "Pressing Share again for the same room hands you back the address you already have, rather than a second one. That is what makes revoking it a whole answer: there is one link to close, not an unknown number of them. After revoking, Share mints a fresh address — so a link pasted in the wrong place is fixable rather than permanent."
  )}
</p>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_status_user}>{dgettext("help_p2p", "Who can revoke")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_p2p",
    "Your own links are yours. A channel operator can also revoke a link that leads into their channel — a conference in it, or its space — because an address people keep arriving through is the channel's business as much as the room itself is."
  )}
</p>

<p>
  {dgettext("help_p2p", "See also:")}
  <.help_link topic="feature-conference-share">
    {dgettext("help_p2p", "Sharing a Conference Link")}
  </.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="feature-space-share">
    {dgettext("help_p2p", "Sharing a Space")}
  </.help_link>
</p>
